# Baccarat settlement — an ExactOdds casino rule pack.
#
# Baccarat's edge lives in one rule: banker wins pay 19:20, not even money.
# Get the commission wrong and the whole game's math drifts. This program is
# the settlement both the table system and the player's receipt run: stake,
# bet side, and winner in, exact payout in cents out.
#
# Rules: bet_on 0 = player, 1 = banker, 2 = tie; winner uses the same codes.
# A player win pays 1:1. A banker win pays 19:20 (the 5% commission).
# A tie bet pays 8:1; player/banker bets push on a tie — stake back.
# A losing side pays 0. Integer cents, no floats — floats can't be exact.

def baccarat_settle(stake_cents: int, bet_on: int, winner: int) -> int do
    if winner == 2 do
        if bet_on == 2 do
            ret stake_cents + stake_cents * 8
        end
        ret stake_cents
    end
    if bet_on == winner do
        if bet_on == 1 do
            ret stake_cents + stake_cents * 19 / 20
        end
        ret stake_cents * 2
    end
    ret 0
end

# Audited cases: $10 stake.
say(baccarat_settle(1000, 0, 0))
say(baccarat_settle(1000, 1, 1))
say(baccarat_settle(1000, 2, 2))
say(baccarat_settle(1000, 0, 2))
say(baccarat_settle(1000, 1, 0))
